  "slug": "in-process-quality-production-log-form",
  "title": "In-Process Quality Production Log Form",
  "subtitle": "Control the starting state, record chronological in-process inspection and control check activity, reconcile quantities and holds, authorize restarts, and hand off the next due check.",
  "description": "A chronological in-process quality production log form for reconstructing how a work-in-process lot or serial range moved through readiness, execution, interruptions, measurements, quantity reconciliation, exceptions, restart decisions, and shift closeout.",
  "use_case": "Use during active in-process inspection and control check work when operators and reviewers need a time-ordered trace that identifies who did what, the actual result, affected range, and last known acceptable status.",
  "risk_tier": "A",
